{"id":"cost-management","corpus":"aws","title":"AWS Cost Management","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/what-is-costmanagement.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"AWS Cost Management"},{"kind":"p","text":"Welcome to the AWS Cost Management User Guide."},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS Billing and Cost Management provides a suite of features to help you set up your billing, retrieve and pay invoices, and analyze, organize, plan, and optimize your costs."},{"kind":"p","text":"To get started, set up your billing to match your requirements. For individuals or small organizations, AWS will automatically charge the credit card provided."},{"kind":"p","text":"For larger organizations, you can use AWS Organizations to consolidate your charges across multiple AWS accounts. You can then configure invoicing, tax, purchase order, and payment methods to match your organization’s procurement processes."},{"kind":"p","text":"If you have multiple AWS Organizations, use billing transfer to centrally manage and pay for all your organizations from a single account."},{"kind":"p","text":"You can allocate your costs to teams, applications, or environments by using cost categories or cost allocation tags, or using AWS Cost Explorer. You can also export data to your preferred data warehouse or business intelligence tool."},{"kind":"p","text":"See the following overview of features to help you manage your cloud finances."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Features of AWS Billing and Cost Management"},{"kind":"h3","text":"Billing and payments"},{"kind":"p","text":"Understand your monthly charges, view and pay invoices, and manage preferences for billing, invoices, tax, and payments."},{"kind":"li","text":"Bills page – Download invoices and view detailed monthly billing data to understand how your charges were calculated."},{"kind":"li","text":"Purchase orders – Create and manage your purchase orders to comply with your organization’s unique procurement processes."},{"kind":"li","text":"Payments – Understand your outstanding or past-due payment balance and payment history."},{"kind":"li","text":"Payment profiles – Set up multiple payment methods for different AWS service providers or parts of your organization."},{"kind":"li","text":"Credits – Review credit balances and choose where credits should be applied."},{"kind":"li","text":"Billing preferences – Enable invoice delivery by email and your preferences for credit sharing, alerts, and discount sharing."},{"kind":"li","text":"Billing transfer – Separates billing and financial management from security and governance management. This enables a single AWS organization to get centralized access to cost data and AWS invoices across multiple AWS organizations."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Cost analysis"},{"kind":"p","text":"Analyze your costs, export detailed cost and usage data, and forecast your spending."},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS Cost Explorer – Analyze your cost and usage data with visuals, filtering, and grouping. You can forecast your costs and create custom reports."},{"kind":"li","text":"Data exports – Create custom data exports from Billing and Cost Management datasets."},{"kind":"li","text":"Cost Anomaly Detection – Set up automated alerts when AWS detects a cost anomaly to reduce unexpected costs."},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS Free Tier – Monitor current and forecasted usage of free tier services to avoid unexpected costs."},{"kind":"li","text":"Split cost allocation data – Enable detailed cost and usage data for shared Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) resources."},{"kind":"li","text":"Cost Management preferences – Manage what data that member accounts can view, change account data granularity, and configure cost optimization preferences."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Cost organization"},{"kind":"p","text":"Organize your costs across teams, applications, or end customers."},{"kind":"li","text":"Cost categories – Map costs to teams, applications, or environments, and then view costs along these dimensions in Cost Explorer and data exports. Define split charge rules to allocate shared costs."},{"kind":"li","text":"Cost allocation tags – Use resource tags to organize, and then view costs by cost allocation tag in Cost Explorer and data exports."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Budgeting and planning"},{"kind":"p","text":"Estimate the cost of a planned workload, and create budgets to track and control costs."},{"kind":"li","text":"Budgets – Set custom budgets for cost and usage to govern costs across your organization and receive alerts when costs exceed your defined thresholds."},{"kind":"li","text":"In-console Pricing calculator – Use this feature to estimate your planned cloud costs using your discount and purchase commitments."},{"kind":"li","text":"Public Pricing calculator website – Create cost estimates for using AWS services with On-Demand rates."},{"kind":"h3","text":"Savings and commitments"},{"kind":"p","text":"Optimize resource usage and use flexible pricing models to lower your bill."},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS Cost Optimization Hub – Identify savings opportunities with tailored recommendations including deleting unused resources, rightsizing, Savings Plans, and reservations."},{"kind":"li","text":"Savings Plans – Reduce your bill compared to On-Demand prices with flexible pricing models. Manage your Savings Plans inventory, review purchase recommendations, run purchase analyses, and analyze Savings Plans utilization and coverage."},{"kind":"li","text":"Reservations – Reserve capacity at discounted rates for Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2), Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS), Amazon Redshift, Amazon DynamoDB, and more."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Related services"},{"kind":"h3","text":"AWS Billing Conductor"},{"kind":"p","text":"Billing Conductor is a custom billing service that supports the showback and chargeback workflows of AWS Partners reselling AWS services, solutions, and AWS customers purchasing cloud services directly through AWS. You can customize a second, alternative version of your monthly billing data. The service models the billing relationship between you and your customers or business units."}],"lemmas":{"costing":["costing","cost"],"managements":["management","managements"],"welcomes":["welcome","welcomes"],"welcomed":["welcomed","welcome"],"welcoming":["welcoming","welcome"],"users":["user","users"],"guides":["guide","guides"],"guided":["guided","guide"],"guiding":["guiding","guide"],"billing":["billing","bill"],"billings":["billing","billings"],"billed":["billed","bill"],"provides":["provides","provide"],"providing":["providing","provide"],"suites":["suite","suit","suites"],"features":["feature","features"],"featuring":["featuring","feature"],"featured":["featured","feature"],"helps":["help","helps"],"helping":["helping","help"],"helped":["helped","help"],"sets":["set","sets"],"setting":["setting","set"],"retrieves":["retrieves","retrieve"],"pays":["pay","pays"],"paying":["paying","pay"],"paid":["paid","pay"],"invoices":["invoice","invoices"],"analyzes":["analyzes","analyze"],"analyzed":["analyzed","analyze"],"analyzing":["analyzing","analyze"],"organizes":["organizes","organize"],"organized":["organized","organize"],"organizing":["organizing","organize"],"planed":["planed","plan"],"optimizes":["optimizes","optimize"],"costs":["cost","costs"],"started":["started","start"],"starteds":["starteds","started"],"starts":["start","starts"],"starting":["starting","start"],"matches":["match","matches"],"matched":["matched","match"],"matching":["matching","match"],"requirements":["requirement","requirements"],"individuals":["individual","individuals"],"smalls":["small","smalls"],"smaller":["smaller","small"],"organizations":["organization","organizations"],"wills":["will","wills"],"willing":["willing","will"],"willed":["willed","will"],"would":["would","will"],"automaticallies":["automaticallies","automatically"],"ch